    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "comment-1",
        "text": "FORMATTING TEXT\n\nNumber To String and Bool To String make text from other values (a value wired straight into a String\npin is converted automatically too). Justify nodes pad text to a width, which is how you line up\ncolumns or zero-pad numbers; String Repeat makes rulers and borders.",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          -300.0
        ],
        "size": [
          900.0,
          170.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.4,
          0.8,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-2",
        "text": "Each node's literal inputs are typed on the node. Expected: \"3.5\", \"true\", \"007\" (right-justified to width 3 with '0'), left-justified \"ab...\", centered \"**hi**\"-style padding, \"ababab\". The last node prints the zero-padded value.",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          -70.0
        ],
        "size": [
